cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Host and viral mechanisms of ripening impairment in grapevine red blotch disease across source leaves and developing berries"
message: "If this code contributes to published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Prem Pratap
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7921-9379"
    affiliation: "Department of Plant Pathology, University of California, Davis"
repository-code: "https://github.com/prem-p-singh/GRBV-Transcriptomics-Analysis"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - grapevine red blotch virus
  - Vitis vinifera
  - viral pathogenesis
  - berry ripening
  - post-transcriptional gene silencing
  - small heat-shock proteins
  - 3-prime TAG-seq
  - digital PCR
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis and manuscript pipeline for a longitudinal cross-tissue study
  of grapevine red blotch virus (GRBV) in field-grown Vitis vinifera L. cv. Merlot
  (clone 12 on 1103P rootstock, Paso Robles, CA): 327 UMI-deduplicated 3' TAG-seq
  berry pericarp libraries from 44 vines (36 GRBV-positive, 8 GRBV-negative) across
  four phenological stages and two seasons (2021 and 2022), integrated with harvest
  must chemistry and 267 vine-matched leaf-petiole QuantStudio 3D digital PCR viral
  DNA assays. An uncensored healthy-vine developmental reference and external MPhS
  projection separate delayed berry maturation from maturation-independent host and
  viral C2 transcriptional pathology.
